---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Terms and Conditions | BitsNotes" 
  description="Read the BitsNotes Terms and Conditions to understand the rules, responsibilities, and limitations that govern your use of our educational platform."
  keywords="bitsnotes terms and conditions, terms of service, educational platform terms, legal terms, DMCA policy"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Terms and Conditions",
      "description": "BitsNotes Terms and Conditions governing use of the educational platform, content usage, and intellectual property.",
      "url": "https://bitsnotes.com/terms"
    })} />
  </Fragment>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16 flex-grow">
    
    <!-- Title Header -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-12">
      <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 uppercase tracking-widest bg-indigo-50 dark:bg-indigo-950/50 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg mb-4">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Terms and Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-base md:text-lg">
        Last updated: June 2, 2026. By accessing BitsNotes, you agree to the following terms governing your use of our platform.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content Box -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl border border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80 p-8 md:p-12 shadow-xl shadow-slate-100/40 dark:shadow-none space-y-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed reveal-on-scroll">

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using BitsNotes (the "Platform"), you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions and all applicable laws and regulations. If you do not agree with any of these terms, you are prohibited from using or accessing this site. The materials contained in this Platform are protected by applicable copyright and trademark law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Use of Educational Content</h2>
        <p>
          BitsNotes provides lecture notes, study guides, and educational materials (collectively, "Content") exclusively for personal, non-commercial educational use. You are permitted to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>View Content within the Platform's viewer for personal study purposes.</li>
          <li>Access materials as an authorised user.</li>
          <li>Use Content to supplement your academic learning and exam preparation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You are expressly prohibited from downloading, reproducing, distributing, publishing, or creating derivative works from any Content without prior written permission from BitsNotes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          All Content, design elements, trademarks, and intellectual property on BitsNotes are the exclusive property of BitsNotes or its content providers and are protected by Indian and international copyright and intellectual property laws. Unauthorised use of any materials may violate copyright, trademark, and other applicable laws and could result in legal action.
        </p>
        <p>
          The BitsNotes name, logo, and all related product and service names, design marks, and slogans are trademarks of BitsNotes. You may not use these marks without the prior written permission of BitsNotes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">4. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p>When using BitsNotes, you agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>Attempt to circumvent, reverse-engineer, or disable any access-control features on the Platform.</li>
          <li>Use automated tools, bots, scrapers, or scripts to extract or download Content.</li>
          <li>Share, resell, or redistribute any downloaded or screen-captured content from the Platform.</li>
          <li>Impersonate any person or entity or misrepresent your affiliation with any person or entity.</li>
          <li>Upload or transmit viruses or any other type of malicious code.</li>
          <li>Engage in any activity that disrupts or interferes with the Platform's servers or networks.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The Content on BitsNotes is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis for educational and informational purposes only. BitsNotes makes no representations or warranties of any kind, express or implied, regarding the accuracy, completeness, reliability, or suitability of the Content for any particular purpose. 
        </p>
        <p>
          While we strive to keep all lecture notes and study materials accurate and up-to-date, BitsNotes does not guarantee that all Content is error-free. We strongly encourage you to verify important information from official academic sources and your institution's authorised materials.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, BitsNotes and its operators, employees, and affiliates shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your access to or use of (or inability to access or use) the Platform or its Content, including but not limited to damages for loss of data, academic performance, or goodwill.
        </p>
        <p>
          In no event shall BitsNotes's total liability to you for all damages exceed the amount you have paid BitsNotes in the last six (6) months (which, as BitsNotes is a free service, shall be zero).
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">7. Third-Party Links and Advertisements</h2>
        <p>
          BitsNotes may display third-party advertisements served by Google AdSense and may contain links to external websites. These third-party sites have separate and independent privacy policies and terms of service. We have no responsibility or liability for the content or activities of these linked sites.
        </p>
        <p>
          The inclusion of any link does not imply endorsement by BitsNotes. We encourage you to review the terms and privacy policies of any third-party website you visit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">8. Content Accuracy and Updates</h2>
        <p>
          BitsNotes reserves the right to modify, update, or remove any Content at any time without notice. Lecture notes and educational materials may be updated periodically to reflect syllabus changes or corrections. It is your responsibility to check for the most current version of any material before your examinations or assessments.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">9. DMCA and Copyright Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe that any Content on BitsNotes infringes upon your copyright, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:support@bitsnotes.example.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-bold hover:underline">support@bitsnotes.example.com</a> with the following information:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li>A description of the copyrighted work you claim has been infringed.</li>
          <li>The URL or location of the allegedly infringing material on our Platform.</li>
          <li>Your contact information (name, address, phone number, and email).</li>
          <li>A statement that you have a good faith belief that the use is not authorised by the copyright owner.</li>
          <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in your notice is accurate.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We will promptly investigate all valid DMCA notices and take appropriate action, including removal of infringing content where required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">10. Modifications to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          BitsNotes reserves the right to revise these Terms and Conditions at any time. We will indicate the date of the last update at the top of this page. By continuing to use the Platform after any changes are posted, you accept and agree to the revised terms. It is your responsibility to review these Terms periodically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">11. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms and Conditions shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India, without regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any disputes arising under or in connection with these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of India.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800/80" />

      <section class="space-y-3 reveal-on-scroll">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">12. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about these Terms and Conditions, please contact us at:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-indigo-50/60 dark:bg-indigo-950/30 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-indigo-100 dark:border-indigo-900/50 text-sm space-y-1">
          <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-white">BitsNotes Support Team</p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@bitsnotes.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-bold hover:underline">support@bitsnotes.com</a></p>
          <p>Website: <a href="/" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-bold hover:underline">BitsNotes Platform</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  const obs = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add('revealed'); });
  }, { threshold: 0.1, rootMargin: '0px 0px -40px 0px' });
  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal-on-scroll').forEach(el => obs.observe(el));
</script>
